                <pb facs="0883" n="871" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg871"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">622.116/121: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-08-19T18:00:00-05:00">August 19, 1940—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>188. Reference to Department’s 116, August 17, 11 a.m. The Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs and the Director General of exchange control out of city. Matter will be
                    further discussed tomorrow or Wednesday and indications are that application of
                    exchange authorizations will be postponed for 2 weeks or longer.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
